                <pb facs="0242" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg130"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 180/48 A.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    Dawson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-07-23"><hi rendition="#italic">July 23,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>President Montt, of Chile, will arrive at Panama on the 25th or 26th instant on
                    board the Chilean warship <hi rendition="#italic">Esmeralda</hi>, on his way to
                        <pb facs="0243" n="131" xml:id="pg131"/> Europe for the benefit of his
                    health. You will cooperate with the authorities of the Canal Zone and exert
                    every effort to make his stay in Panama as agreeable as possible and to
                    facilitate the ease of his transit across the territory of Panama.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
